<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <!--
    The Sessions module's public surface — everything a host, an adapter or
    this context's own UI is allowed to see (ADR 0005, ADR 0009):
      IAgentSessionSource   the port: what sessions an environment has a record of
      AgentSession etc.     the DTOs and enums in that port's signatures
      AgentSessionStates    when a live session stops counting as live — the
                            threshold policy, which the control library explicitly
                            refuses to own because a policy needs a clock
      AgentSessionGroups    the grouping derivation, pure over the sessions it is
                            given
      AgentSessionLimits    how many sessions per agent a source will describe
      SessionFeatures  the key the Shell gates the area on

    The grouping sits here for the same reason EntryTextParser sits in Backlog's
    abstractions: it is the definition two callers would otherwise each write, so
    it is a contract rather than one surface's private detail. Unlike that
    precedent it is genuinely pure — no clock, no I/O, no state — which is what
    lets it be tested without a filesystem underneath it.

    There is no implementation project yet, and that is a statement about how far
    this context has been built rather than a missing piece. Every session fact
    comes from a file an agent already wrote, so the readers that answer the port
    are host-owned adapters; nothing has yet needed a decision that belongs to
    neither a host nor this contract. ModuleSurfaceTests says the same thing about
    the other contexts in this position: demanding a module project for a module
    nobody has written would only produce an empty one.
  -->
  <PropertyGroup>
    <RootNamespace>Backlog.Modules.Sessions.Abstractions</RootNamespace>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!-- The stale-session boundary and the grouping decide what a reader sees as
         running and how the list is carved up, so they are worth testing directly
         rather than only through whichever surface happens to render them. -->
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Backlog.Desktop.UI.UnitTests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
